    {
      "id": "claim_e58ccba9de194c578c3734ff4425743c",
      "statement": "Overload behavior: celld admits a maximum of 64 concurrent fetch events per Durable Object or Queue broker (CELLD_MAX_CELL_REQUESTS), returns HTTP 503 with Retry-After: 1 and X-Celld-Overload: cell without starting the excess event, emits a cell_overload_refused log event with the cell scope, node, region, in-flight count, and limit, and a fixed-rate client must count the response as rejected work so an immediate retry does not increase the offered rate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L640-L658",
