    {
      "id": "claim_6194e29dc67f428c9bb37fff916befd7",
      "statement": "Two separate memory limits apply: the pressure threshold at 80% of available memory and an absolute cap at 95% of the available memory on the complete cgroup charge to protect the node when shedding cannot return a kernel charge; each limit releases at 80% of its own value so crossing one does not hold the node against the other; CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB=0 disables both, and without readable available memory the cap is 125% of an explicit threshold.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L276-L296",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e68b9d264dcb647db273e771f54184497601626893afb962a9963d8583b406a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d84ff1cc4e6447568bafd314aff14425",
      "statement": "Under pressure celld durably replicates and fences the least-recently-used idle cells, publishes them as unowned without resetting their epochs, and refuses to reacquire new unowned cells; it does not shed a cell with active work or a live host WebSocket, and a spare node receives no assignment but acquires a released cell through the same bucket protocol when normal traffic reaches it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L288-L297",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:63603f9b78fc89455285866655603d2700e5ee903ea9b5debb6ca8bfa4c71add:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2c6f2ee360924f89bdef646dbda89821",
      "statement": "The pressure policy is in the decision core: PressureConfig::from_limits derives thresholds, classify() maps a Load sample and former Latches into new latches with a reason, has_headroom and resume_line supply per-metric release points, and release_target/walk_metric sequence releases; the executor never sheds a cell on its own judgment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L151-L263",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:79010d82f5aa25388c9df447fef698f9d29703a97913c4dde775e9dc9499abd5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ab160b78ccbd4a01a45b727d4adbc749",
      "statement": "Each isolate also has a separate V8 heap limit (default 128 MB matching Cloudflare's Durable Object limit, CELLD_V8_HEAP_LIMIT_MB to change): above 90% the isolate refuses a new hibernatable WebSocket and stops a SQL result-set materialization; it serves again under 90% on both; celld measures the heap before each event and forces a collection when idle measurement is above 75% of the limit, and a process restart is not necessary.",
      "evidence": [
